# Story: somebody has six windows open and cannot find one of them. They know no shortcut and no word of Arbor's. They open the one
# thing of Arbor's that is always there, the menu, read the list under Windows and click: the window is in front and whole,
# whatever kept it out of sight. (QUESTIONS Q29, point 8; IDEAS I17. Window ids start at 101; a window opens as "Mail 102".)
quiet
# As Arbor ships, what cannot fit overlaps (F69). This story is about the tile, which is an option now.
set windowsThatDoNotFit tile
open Safari
open Mail
open Notes
open Terminal 400x300
open Music
open Calendar 500x400
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
dock 103 beside 102 bottom
move 104 520 300 400 300
focus 103
focus 102
focus 101
# The window being typed in is ticked. (That it is first, the others in the order of use, and that a window in view has no mark, no `expect` can
# say: OpenWindowsTests does.)
menu
expect replied ✓ Safari: Safari 101
expect replied Mail: Mail 102
# Framed on Safari, the others are out of view, and the list says so.
zoom 101
expect hidden 102
menu
expect replied Mail: Mail 102  [out of view]
expect replied Notes: Notes 103  [out of view]
# A docked window out of view.
menu-choose Mail
expect ok
expect visible 102
expect focused 102
expect in-front 102
expect moved-once
menu
expect replied ✓ Mail: Mail 102
# A floating window, with another lying over it.
show-all
move 106 500 280 500 400
focus 106
menu-choose Terminal
expect ok
expect still
expect focused 104
expect in-front 104
# One left hanging over the corner of the screen comes in whole, at its own size, by the shortest way.
move 104 1300 780 400 300
focus 101
menu-choose Terminal
expect ok
expect at 104 1040 600
expect size 104 400x300
expect in-front 104
# Out of the Dock, docked and floating.
minimize 103
minimize 106
menu
expect replied Notes: Notes 103  [minimized]
menu-choose Notes
expect ok
expect visible 103
expect focused 103
expect in-front 103
menu-choose Calendar
expect ok
expect visible 106
expect focused 106
expect in-front 106
expect size 106 500x400
# Out of ⌘H.
hide Mail
menu
expect replied Mail: Mail 102  [hidden]
menu-choose Mail
expect ok
expect visible 102
expect focused 102
expect in-front 102
# A window too small to show is drawn as a tile. Whoever looks for it need not know the word.
min 105 1000x700
dock 105 beside 103 bottom
expect tile 105
menu
expect replied Music: Music 105  [out of view]
menu-choose Music
expect ok
expect visible 105
expect focused 105
expect in-front 105
# An app Arbor was told not to arrange is in the list all the same, and is shown where it is.
show-all
exclude com.example.calendar
focus 101
menu-choose Calendar
expect ok
expect focused 106
expect in-front 106
# What has closed is no longer listed.
close 104
menu-choose Terminal
expect fail
